/* ShiroRVC -- the sliver of style that has to be application-wide.
 *
 * Everything else lives in style.qss and is applied to the main window, whose
 * subtree is every widget the user can see.  That scoping is what makes a
 * theme switch 0.3 s instead of 2.1 s: an application-wide sheet makes Qt
 * re-resolve rules for every widget in the process, and there are ~1500.
 *
 * A tooltip is the exception -- it is a top-level widget with no parent, so
 * the window's sheet never reaches it.  Hence this file, which is set once at
 * startup and never again: no literal colour anywhere, only palette roles, so
 * it stays correct in both themes without being re-applied.  Add to it only
 * for things Qt parents to the desktop rather than to us.
 */

QToolTip {
    background: palette(button);
    color: palette(button-text);
    border: 1px solid palette(mid);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 5px 8px;
}
